  "name": "Answer WhatsApp shop messages and log orders to Google Sheets with Claude and Twilio",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "7232b457-61c6-5af7-9b67-bfa50cb45e6e",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -760,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1280,
        "content": "## Answer WhatsApp shop messages and log orders\n\nA WhatsApp order desk for small shops. Every message is sorted by AI into order, question, complaint, social or other, answered in your shop's voice, and logged to Google Sheets.\n\n### How it works\n1. Twilio forwards each WhatsApp message to the webhook.\n2. Claude Haiku classifies the message.\n3. **Orders:** details are extracted, saved to the Orders tab and confirmed.\n4. **Questions:** answered only from your FAQ tab, never invented.\n5. **Complaints:** logged, acknowledged with a same-day follow-up promise, and emailed to you.\n6. Social chat gets a short friendly reply; anything else goes to the Review tab.\n7. The reply goes back on WhatsApp.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a Google Sheet with tabs **Orders**, **FAQ**, **Complaints** and **Review**. Each Sheets node's note lists its row-1 headers. Add a few FAQ rows.\n2. Fill in **Settings**: shop name, what you sell, links, alert email and the sheet ID.\n3. Add credentials: Anthropic (6 Claude nodes), Google Sheets (4), Gmail (1), Twilio (1).\n4. Activate, then paste the production webhook URL into your Twilio WhatsApp sender (or the free WhatsApp Sandbox) as the incoming-message URL (POST).\n5. Send a test message.\n6. Optional security: paste your Twilio Auth Token and the production webhook URL into **Settings**. Requests not signed by Twilio are then rejected.\n\n### Customization tips\nEdit the FAQ tab to change answers without touching the workflow. Add a category by extending the classifier prompt and the Switch.\n\n_Built by Alicia Graham, economist and n8n Ambassador._"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
